msgstr ""
"Cette variable correspond au paramètre 'B<live-config.user-dirs-"
"path>=I<CHEMIN>'. Elle spécifie le chemin des répertoires d'utilisateurs sur "
"le média."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:267
msgid ""
"User-media link and bind modes are mutually exclusive. The default path is /"
"minios/userdata relative to the existing /run/initramfs/memory/data mount.  "
"Only writable local block-backed FAT32, exFAT, and NTFS media are accepted.  "
"Network, optical, RAM, overlay, read-only, unsupported filesystems, and "
"toram, toram=full, or toram=trim are rejected. Paths may not contain "
"traversal, empty segments, control characters, or unsafe names. Desktop, "
"Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures, Public, Templates, and Videos are "
"managed. Migration refuses to merge two populated trees; disabling the "
"feature copies managed data back.  State and status are recorded under /var/"
"lib/live/config."
msgstr ""
"Les modes de liaison et de montage utilisateur-média sont mutuellement "
"exclusifs. Le chemin par défaut est /minios/userdata, relatif au point de "
"montage /run/initramfs/memory/data existant. Seuls les supports locaux en "
"écriture de type FAT32, exFAT et NTFS avec support bloc sont acceptés. Les "
"supports réseau, optiques, RAM, overlay, en lecture seule, systèmes de "
"fichiers non pris en charge, ainsi que toram, toram=full ou toram=trim sont "
"rejetés. Les chemins ne doivent pas contenir de traversée, de segments "
"vides, de caractères de contrôle ou de noms non sûrs. Les répertoires "
"Desktop, Documents, Downloads, Music, Pictures, Public, Templates et Videos "
"sont gérés. La migration refuse de fusionner deux arborescences déjà "
"peuplées ; la désactivation de la fonctionnalité copie les données gérées en "
"retour. L'état et le statut sont enregistrés sous /var/lib/live/config."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<LIVE_MODULE_MODE>=simple|merged"
msgstr "B<LIVE_MODULE_MODE>=simple|merged"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:269
msgid ""
"This variable holds the state specified by the 'live-config.module-mode' (or "
"'module-mode') parameter. When it is set to \"merged\", the live system "
"applies updates (via minios-update-users, minios-update-cache, and minios-"
"update-dpkg) to merge custom configurations with the base environment."
msgstr ""
"Cette variable contient l'état défini par le paramètre 'live-config.module-"
"mode' (ou 'module-mode'). Lorsqu'il est réglé sur \"merged\", le système en "
"direct applique des mises à jour (via minios-update-users, minios-update-"
"cache et minios-update-dpkg) pour fusionner les configurations "
"personnalisées avec l'environnement de base."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:269
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<LIVE_CONFIG_DEBUG>=true|false"
msgstr "B<LIVE_CONFIG_DEBUG>=true|false"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:271
msgid "This variable corresponds to the 'B<live-config.debug>' parameter."
msgstr "Cette variable correspond au paramètre 'B<live-config.debug>'."

#. type: SH
#: en/live-config.7:272
#, no-wrap
msgid "CUSTOMIZATION"
msgstr "PERSONNALISATION"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:274
msgid ""
"B<live-config> can be easily customized for downstream projects or local "
"usage."
msgstr ""
"B<live-config> peut être facilement personnalisé pour des projets dérivés, "
"ou pour un usage local."

#. type: SS
#: en/live-config.7:275
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding new config components"
msgstr "Ajout de nouveaux composants de configuration"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:277
msgid ""
"Downstream projects can put their components into /usr/lib/live/config and "
"do not need to do anything else, the components will be called automatically "
"during boot."
msgstr ""
"Les projets dérivés peuvent utiliser leurs propres composants dans /lib/live/"
"config et n'ont besoin de rien d'autre, les composants seront appelés lors "
"du démarrage."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:279
msgid ""
"The components are best put into an own debian package. A sample package "
"containing an example component can be found in /usr/share/doc/live-config/"
"examples."
msgstr ""
"Il est préférable que les composants soient mis dans leur propre paquet "
"Debian. Un paquet contenant un composant d'exemple est proposé dans /usr/"
"share/doc/live-config/examples."

#. type: SS
#: en/live-config.7:280
#, no-wrap
msgid "Removing existing config components"
msgstr "Enlever des composants de configuration existants"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:282
msgid ""
"It is not really possible to remove components itself in a sane way yet "
"without requiring either to ship a locally modified B<live-config> package "
"or using dpkg-divert. However, the same can be achieved by disabling the "
"respective components through the live-config.nocomponents mechanism, see "
"above. To avoid to always need specifying disabled components through the "
"boot parameter, a configuration file should be used, see above."
msgstr ""
"Il n'est actuellement pas vraiment possible d'enlever proprement les "
"composants sans avoir besoin soit d'utiliser un paquet B<live-config> "
"modifié localement, soit à l'aide de dpkg-divert. Cependant, la même chose "
"peut être réalisée en désactivant les scripts respectifs via le mécanisme "
"live-config.nocomponents, comme indiqué ci-dessus. Afin d'éviter de toujours "
"avoir à spécifier les composants désactivés via le paramètre d'amorçage, un "
"fichier de configuration devrait être utilisé, voir ci-dessus."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:284
msgid ""
"The configuration files for the live system itself are best put into an own "
"debian package. A sample package containing an example configuration can be "
"found in /usr/share/doc/live-config/examples."
msgstr ""
"Les fichiers de configuration pour le système live lui-même devront de "
"préférence être inclus dans leur propre paquet debian. Un paquet de "
"démonstration contenant un exemple de configuration est proposé dans /usr/"
"share/doc/live-config/examples."

#. type: SH
#: en/live-config.7:285
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMPONENTS"
msgstr "COMPOSANTS"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:287
msgid ""
"B<live-config> currently features the following components in /usr/lib/live/"
"config."
msgstr ""
"B<live-config> fournit actuellement les composants suivants dans /lib/live/"
"config."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:288
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<nss-systemd>"
msgstr "B<nss-systemd>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:290
msgid ""
"removes or restores the systemd NSS module in /etc/nsswitch.conf to work "
"around a known systemd issue."
msgstr ""
"supprime ou restaure le module NSS de systemd dans /etc/nsswitch.conf pour "
"contourner un problème connu de systemd."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:290
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<debconf>"
msgstr "B<debconf>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:292
msgid ""
"allows one to apply arbitrary preseed files placed on the live media or an "
"http/ftp server."
msgstr ""
"permet d'appliquer des fichiers de pré-configuration arbitraires placés sur "
"les média live ou un serveur http/ftp."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<hostname>"
msgstr "B<hostname>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:294
msgid "configures /etc/hostname and /etc/hosts."
msgstr "configure /etc/hostname et /etc/hosts."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:294
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<issue-setup>"
msgstr "B<issue-setup>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:296
msgid ""
"sets up the /etc/issue file with a welcome banner and distribution "
"information."
msgstr ""
"configure le fichier /etc/issue avec une bannière de bienvenue et des "
"informations de distribution."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:296
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<live-debconfig_passwd>"
msgstr "B<live-debconfig_passwd>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:298
msgid "configures user and root passwords via live-debconfig."
msgstr ""
"configure les mots de passe de l'utilisateur et de root via live-debconfig."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:298
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<user-setup>"
msgstr "B<user-setup>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:300
msgid "adds a live user account."
msgstr "ajoute un compte d'utilisateur live."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<user-groups>"
msgstr "B<user-groups>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:302
msgid ""
"adds the live user to supplementary groups declared by installed modules. "
"Existing groups listed in /usr/share/live/config/user-default-groups.d/"
"*.groups are applied after user creation and on later live-config runs."
msgstr ""
"ajoute l'utilisateur live aux groupes supplémentaires déclarés par les "
"modules installés. Les groupes existants listés dans /usr/share/live/config/"
"user-default-groups.d/*.groups sont appliqués après la création de "
"l'utilisateur et lors des exécutions ultérieures de live-config."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:302
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<root-setup>"
msgstr "B<root-setup>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:304
msgid ""
"sets or updates the root password and configures the root user environment."
msgstr ""
"définit ou met à jour le mot de passe de root et configure l'environnement "
"de l'utilisateur root."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:304
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sudo>"
msgstr "B<sudo>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:306
msgid "grants sudo privileges to the live user."
msgstr "offre les privilèges sudo à l'utilisateur live."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<user-ssh-keys>"
msgstr "B<user-ssh-keys>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:308
msgid ""
"synchronizes user-specific I<authorized_keys.E<lt>usernameE<gt>> files "
"between the live medium and individual user home directories. Supports "
"multiple users simultaneously (e.g., I<authorized_keys.root>, "
"I<authorized_keys.live>, I<authorized_keys.admin>)."
msgstr ""
"synchronise les fichiers I<authorized_keys.E<lt>usernameE<gt>> spécifiques à "
"chaque utilisateur entre le support live et les répertoires personnels des "
"utilisateurs. Prend en charge plusieurs utilisateurs simultanément (par "
"exemple, I<authorized_keys.root>, I<authorized_keys.live>, "
"I<authorized_keys.admin>)."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:308
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<user-media>"
msgstr "B<user-media>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:311
msgid ""
"links or bind-mounts validated user directories on the existing writable "
"MiniOS data medium, with safe migration and copy-back when disabled."
msgstr ""
"lie ou monte en mode bind les répertoires utilisateur validés sur le support "
"de données MiniOS existant en écriture, avec migration sécurisée et copie de "
"retour lors de la désactivation."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:311
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<locales>"
msgstr "B<locales>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:313
msgid "configures locales."
msgstr "configure les locales."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:313
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<tzdata>"
msgstr "B<tzdata>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:315
msgid "configures /etc/timezone."
msgstr "configure /etc/timezone."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:315
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xorg-service>"
msgstr "B<xorg-service>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:317
msgid ""
"configures username in xorg.service and applies X11 posture when supported."
msgstr ""
"configure le nom d'utilisateur dans xorg.service et applique la posture X11 "
"lorsque cela est pris en charge."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:317
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<gdm3>"
msgstr "B<gdm3>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:319
msgid "configures autologin in gdm3."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans gdm3."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sddm>"
msgstr "B<sddm>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:321
msgid "configures autologin in sddm."
msgstr "configure la connexion automatique dans sddm."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:321
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<kdm>"
msgstr "B<kdm>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:323
msgid "configures autologin in kdm."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans kdm."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:323
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<lightdm>"
msgstr "B<lightdm>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:325
msgid "configures autologin in lightdm."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans lightdm."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:325
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<lxdm>"
msgstr "B<lxdm>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:327
msgid "configures autologin in lxdm."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans lxdm."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:327
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<nodm>"
msgstr "B<nodm>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:329
msgid "configures autologin in nodm."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans nodm."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:329
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<slim>"
msgstr "B<slim>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:331
msgid "configures autologin in slim."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login dans slim."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:331
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xinit>"
msgstr "B<xinit>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:333
msgid "configures autologin with xinit."
msgstr "configure l'auto-login avec xinit."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<keyboard-configuration>"
msgstr "B<keyboard-configuration>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:335
msgid "configures the keyboard."
msgstr "configure le clavier."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:335
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sysvinit>"
msgstr "B<sysvinit>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:338
msgid ""
"configures console autologin through /etc/inittab when sysvinit is "
"installed.  The noautologin and nottyautologin shortcuts suppress that setup."
msgstr ""
"configure la connexion automatique sur la console via /etc/inittab lorsque "
"sysvinit est installé. Les raccourcis noautologin et nottyautologin "
"désactivent cette configuration."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:338
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<sysv-rc>"
msgstr "B<sysv-rc>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:340
msgid "configures sysv-rc by disabling listed services."
msgstr "configure sysv-rc en désactivant les services listés."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<apport>"
msgstr "B<apport>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:342
msgid "disables apport."
msgstr "désactive apport."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:342
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<gnome-panel-data>"
msgstr "B<gnome-panel-data>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:344
msgid "disables lock button for the screen."
msgstr "désactive le bouton de verrouillage de l'écran."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:344
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<gnome-power-manager>"
msgstr "B<gnome-power-manager>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:346
msgid "disables hibernation."
msgstr "désactive l'hibernation."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:346
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<gnome-screensaver>"
msgstr "B<gnome-screensaver>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:348
msgid "controls GNOME screen locking according to LIVE_LOCKSCREEN_MODE."
msgstr "contrôle le verrouillage d'écran GNOME selon LIVE_LOCKSCREEN_MODE."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:348
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<kaboom>"
msgstr "B<kaboom>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:350
msgid "disables KDE migration wizard (squeeze and newer)."
msgstr "désactive l'assistant de migration de KDE (squeeze et plus récent)."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:350
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<kde-services>"
msgstr "B<kde-services>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:352
msgid "disables some unwanted KDE services (squeeze and newer)."
msgstr "désactive des services de KDE non souhaités (squeeze et plus récent)."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:352
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<policykit>"
msgstr "B<policykit>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:354
msgid "grants user privileges through PolicyKit."
msgstr "octroie les privilèges utilisateur via PolicyKit."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:354
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ssl-cert>"
msgstr "B<ssl-cert>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:356
msgid "regenerates SSL snake-oil certificates."
msgstr "régénère les certificats SSL snake-oil."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:356
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xrdp>"
msgstr "B<xrdp>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:358
msgid ""
"configures relaxed, hardened, or disabled XRDP posture when XRDP is "
"installed."
msgstr ""
"configure la posture XRDP relâchée, renforcée ou désactivée lorsque XRDP est "
"installé."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:358
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<anacron>"
msgstr "B<anacron>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:360
msgid "disables anacron."
msgstr "désactive anacron."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:360
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<util-linux>"
msgstr "B<util-linux>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:362
msgid "disables the util-linux hwclock service."
msgstr "désactive le service hwclock de util-linux."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:362
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<login>"
msgstr "B<login>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:364
msgid "disables lastlog."
msgstr "désactive lastlog."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:364
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xserver-xorg>"
msgstr "B<xserver-xorg>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:366
msgid "configures xserver-xorg."
msgstr "configure xserver-xorg."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:366
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<network>"
msgstr "B<réseau>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:368
msgid ""
"configures durable wired IPv4 policy through a secure NetworkManager keyfile "
"or ifupdown stanza. It runs before networking services, validates all "
"values, and stamps only after a successful write."
msgstr ""
"configure une politique IPv4 filaire durable via un fichier clé sécurisé "
"NetworkManager ou une strophe ifupdown. S'exécute avant les services réseau, "
"valide toutes les valeurs et n'applique la configuration qu'après une "
"écriture réussie."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:368
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<openssh-server>"
msgstr "B<openssh-server>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:371
msgid ""
"recreates OpenSSH host keys and writes explicitly requested root-login or "
"password-authentication policy."
msgstr ""
"recrée les clés hôtes OpenSSH et applique explicitement la politique "
"demandée pour la connexion root ou l'authentification par mot de passe."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:371
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xfce4-panel>"
msgstr "B<xfce4-panel>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:373
msgid "configures xfce4-panel to default settings."
msgstr "configure xfce4-panel avec les réglages par défaut."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:373
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<xscreensaver>"
msgstr "B<xscreensaver>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:375
msgid "controls xscreensaver locking according to LIVE_LOCKSCREEN_MODE."
msgstr "contrôle le verrouillage xscreensaver selon LIVE_LOCKSCREEN_MODE."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:375
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<broadcom-sta>"
msgstr "B<broadcom-sta>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:377
msgid "configures broadcom-sta WLAN drivers."
msgstr "configure les pilotes WLAN broadcom-sta."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:377
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<hyperv>"
msgstr "B<hyperv>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:379
msgid ""
"configures X11 settings to improve compatibility on Microsoft Hyper-V "
"platforms."
msgstr ""
"configure les paramètres X11 pour améliorer la compatibilité sur les "
"plateformes Microsoft Hyper-V."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:379
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ntfs3>"
msgstr "B<ntfs3>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:381
msgid "manages udev rules for NTFS3 support."
msgstr "gère les règles udev pour le support NTFS3."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:381
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<config-module-mode>"
msgstr "B<config-module-mode>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:383
msgid ""
"configures system module mode and updates caches, user settings, and dpkg."
msgstr ""
"configure le mode module système et met à jour les caches, les paramètres "
"utilisateur et dpkg."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:383
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<hooks>"
msgstr "B<hooks>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:385
msgid ""
"allows one to run arbitrary commands from a file placed on the live media or "
"an http/ftp server."
msgstr ""
"permet de lancer des commandes arbitraires depuis un composant placé sur le "
"média live, ou sur un serveur http/ftp."

#. type: SH
#: en/live-config.7:386
#, no-wrap
msgid "FILES"
msgstr "FICHIERS"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:387
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</etc/live/config.conf>"
msgstr "B</etc/live/config.conf>"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:388
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</etc/live/config.conf.d/*.conf>"
msgstr "B</etc/live/config.conf.d/*.conf>"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:389
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<minios/config.conf>"
msgstr "B<minios/config.conf>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:391
msgid ""
"Configuration file on the live medium, copied to /etc/live/config.conf only "
"when the destination does not exist."
msgstr ""
"Fichier de configuration sur le support live, copié vers /etc/live/"
"config.conf uniquement si la destination n'existe pas."

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:391
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</usr/lib/live/init-config.sh>"
msgstr "B</usr/lib/live/init-config.sh>"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:392
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</usr/lib/live/config.sh>"
msgstr "B</usr/lib/live/config.sh>"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:393
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</usr/lib/live/config/>"
msgstr "B</usr/lib/live/config/>"

#. type: IP
#: en/live-config.7:394
#, no-wrap
msgid "B</usr/share/live/config/user-default-groups.d/*.groups>"
msgstr "B</usr/share/live/config/user-default-groups.d/*.groups>"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/live-config.7:396
msgid ""
"Module-provided supplementary groups for the live user. Group names may be "
"separated by whitespace; blank lines and comments beginning with # are "
"ignored. Only groups that exist in the running system are applied."
msgstr ""
"Groupes supplémentaires fournis par les modules pour l'utilisateur live. Les "
"noms de groupes peuvent être séparés par des espaces ; les lignes vides et "
"les commentaires commençant par # sont ignorés. Seuls les groupes existant "
